('03bd4418-7aa2-5a43-aac7-de92e7a2b939'::uuid,'est','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"In circle C, AB is a diameter, point Q lies on AB and is not A, B, or C, and m∠AQP = 90°. Which statement concerning these lengths is true?\n[Figure: circle with center C, diameter AB; P on circle above AB; PQ perpendicular to AB at Q.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"(AQ)² + (QB)² = (AP)²"},{"key":"B","text":"(AP)² + (AB)² = (PQ)²"},{"key":"C","text":"AB/PQ = PQ/QB"},{"key":"D","text":"AB/AP = AP/AQ"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"extra.md","source_sha256":"84ca68dc45b2ef2b31ffef4bf4fca4ef2cb3beb1365109214d65e6b7240c41ea","source_question_id":"E-20","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/E-20.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for E-20","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from extra.md (E-20)."'::jsonb),
