('8cc5a492-eeb5-5157-96bc-8ba4804bd3d2'::uuid,'est','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'easy','mcq','"The stem-and-leaf plot below depicts the daily average temperature (rounded to the nearest degree) for Treesville over a two-week period, with weekend leafs — W, X, Y, and Z — absent:\nstem 5: 8, W, 9\nstem 6: X, 2, 4, 4, Y, 6, 6, 9\nstem 7: 7, 7\nstem 8: Z\nIf the median daily temperature was 65°, what could be the mode of the data set?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"59°"},{"key":"B","text":"64°"},{"key":"C","text":"66°"},{"key":"D","text":"77°"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"hard.md","source_sha256":"b0a0fb727049e45d7472b3b33f3d1323a44072e91a6e39f7f1a553d9099f493a","source_question_id":"H-21","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from hard.md (H-21)."'::jsonb),
