('062a7150-8e99-5424-b140-0a6f267780ea'::uuid,'est','"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"If a, b, m and n are integers, m > 0, n < 0, and x² + mx + n = (x + a)(x + b), what must be true of the product and the sum of a and b?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"ab > 0 and a + b > 0"},{"key":"B","text":"ab > 0 and a + b < 0"},{"key":"C","text":"ab < 0 and a + b > 0"},{"key":"D","text":"ab < 0 and a + b < 0"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"hard.md","source_sha256":"b0a0fb727049e45d7472b3b33f3d1323a44072e91a6e39f7f1a553d9099f493a","source_question_id":"H-31","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Polynomials & Quadratic Functions"}'::jsonb,'"C"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from hard.md (H-31)."'::jsonb),
