('456bb69e-07dd-5c01-bd2f-8929ba7b5738'::uuid,'est','"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In a class, 1/8 of the boys and 1/4 of the girls play the piano, and 3 times as many girls as boys play the piano. If there are 100 boys and girls in the class, how many boys play the piano?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"3"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"12"},{"key":"D","text":"24"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"hard.md","source_sha256":"b0a0fb727049e45d7472b3b33f3d1323a44072e91a6e39f7f1a553d9099f493a","source_question_id":"H-36","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Algebra Foundations, Equations & Inequalities"}'::jsonb,'"B"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from hard.md (H-36)."'::jsonb),
('f82159fa-0fb9-57ce-89ae-a3b58e7bd7b1'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In the figure, the sides of squares PQTV and QRST are equal. Starting at P, travelling along the sides of the squares, which path is longest?\n[Figure: two equal squares stacked vertically sharing side QT; P top-left, V top-right, Q middle-left, T middle-right, R bottom-left, S bottom-right.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"P to Q to R to S"},{"key":"B","text":"P to Q to S to R"},{"key":"C","text":"P to Q to T to S"},{"key":"D","text":"P to V to Q to S"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"hard.md","source_sha256":"b0a0fb727049e45d7472b3b33f3d1323a44072e91a6e39f7f1a553d9099f493a","source_question_id":"H-37","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/H-37.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for H-37","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from hard.md (H-37)."'::jsonb),
('f1eb3bd6-a445-5ac2-821c-a11f1771c826'::uuid,'est','"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A basketball player made exactly 80 percent of the shots she was allowed in a foul-shooting contest. She missed the first shot and then made 14 in a row. If she made 2 of her remaining shots and missed the rest, which of the following must be true?\nI. She had 20 shots in all.\nII. She missed 3 of her remaining shots.\nIII. She made 40 percent of her remaining shots."'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"None"},{"key":"B","text":"I and II only"},{"key":"C","text":"II and III only"},{"key":"D","text":"I, II, and III"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"hard.md","source_sha256":"b0a0fb727049e45d7472b3b33f3d1323a44072e91a6e39f7f1a553d9099f493a","source_question_id":"H-38","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics, Probability & Data Analysis"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from hard.md (H-38)."'::jsonb),
